Z||000000||CUTTER||11-17-1999||09:55 PM||||I just noticed a few days ago when I was driving my 87GT that I heard a whistling sound comming from in back of me . I have never heard it before. and when I give it gas it whistles louder, and calms down when I leave off the gas. Is it a bad fuel pump or is it just a really good and clean fuel pump or what? and im using up a little more gas then usuall too, at least I think I am.   Thanks, CUTTER||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-17-1999||11:57 PM||||I had a whistling sound that I could not find but it sounded like it was coming from the engine. It was actually the alternator going bad and producing a whistle in the speakers! Hit the gas, the whistle would get louder! I suppose if the bearing of the alternator is going it would be harder to turn...or it could be an errant vacuum line. Chasing down a vacuum leak, good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||11-18-1999||10:03 AM||||I had a whistling sound arise in high rpms in my first Fiero, a 5-spd 85 2m4. It kinda sounded neat, somewhat like a turbo, but much louder. Oddly, it didn't go away until I replaced the valve cover and gasket! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||11-18-1999||10:47 AM||||I get a whistling sound also but I think mine comes from the supercharger( you normally aspirated peasents you)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Scott2M4||11-18-1999||11:39 AM||||Cutter - someone broke in and put a turbo on your engine!  The bastard ...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Seriously though, I heard a similar whistle/whine/whatever you want to call it in my '87 coupe.  A few days later, the alternator went South on me.||||reg||7
Z||000005||CUTTER||11-18-1999||06:13 PM||||hehehe, Yeah i wish. Hey thanks for the replys. Now if my car dont start in a few days I know where to look 1st. Now my car is leaking coolant. time to take it to the shop!!  thanks again, CUTTER||||reg||1
Z||000006||CUTTER||11-18-1999||09:36 PM||||Well, I found the whistling problem. Its my water pump, when the antifreeze collant was leaking from under the motor, and with the wistling sound, I put 2&2 together and figured its the water pump. Anyone agree or disagree?||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierospeeder||11-18-1999||11:17 PM||||You can do two things, take the belt off and spin the waterpump pulley, if it has a lot of play in it (in and out, up and down) and spins very easily it has gone bad and also rub your hand underneath it to feel if its wet, theres a small hole where the coolant would leak.  Spinning the pulleys to see if it makes noise is another thing to do.  ||||reg||1
